---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import JsonLd from '~/components/common/JsonLd.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Inflatable SUP vs RIB Boat — Which Watercraft Is Right for You?',
  description:
    'Compare inflatable stand-up paddle boards and rigid inflatable boats across portability, performance, cost, and use cases. Choose the right watercraft for your lifestyle.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <JsonLd
    type="Article"
    article={{
      headline: 'Inflatable SUP vs RIB Boat — Which Watercraft Is Right for You?',
      description:
        'Compare inflatable stand-up paddle boards and rigid inflatable boats across portability, performance, cost, and use cases.',
      datePublished: '2026-07-07',
    }}
    data={{ url: 'https://aquafarer.com/compare/sup-vs-rib' }}
  />
  <JsonLd
    type="BreadcrumbList"
    breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Compare', href: '/compare' }, { name: 'SUP vs RIB' }]}
  />
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-24 px-6">
    <a href="/products" class="text-sm text-sky-600 hover:text-sky-700">&larr; Products</a>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Inflatable SUP vs RIB Boat</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-500">
      A practical comparison between two very different watercraft — the portable paddle board and the high-performance
      rigid inflatable boat. Understand which one fits your needs.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Inflatable SUP</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-sky-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Propulsion:</strong> Human-powered with paddle. No fuel, engine, or maintenance costs.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-sky-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Portability:</strong> Deflates to backpack size. Weighs 18-30 lbs. Fits in any car or closet.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-sky-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Cost:</strong> $200-$800 all-in (board, paddle, pump, leash). No ongoing fuel costs.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-sky-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Fitness:</strong> Full-body workout. Core engagement, balance, cardiovascular benefit with every session.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-sky-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Best for:</strong> Fitness paddling, touring, yoga, fishing, family recreation, travel, beginners.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">RIB Boat</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Propulsion:</strong> Outboard motor (15-150+ HP). Requires fuel, oil, and regular engine maintenance.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Portability:</strong> Trailer required. 150-500+ kg. Needs garage, marina, or boat storage.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Cost:</strong> $3,000-$15,000+ (boat + motor + trailer). Ongoing fuel and maintenance costs.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Performance:</strong> 25-40+ knots. Carries multiple passengers and heavy gear. Handles rough water.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 flex-shrink-0"></span><span
              ><strong>Best for:</strong> Offshore cruising, search and rescue, commercial operations, watersports towing,
              group outings.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Side-by-Side Comparison</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b-2 border-gray-200">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-gray-700">Factor</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-center font-semibold text-sky-700">Inflatable SUP</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-center font-semibold text-emerald-700">RIB Boat</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              [
                ['Propulsion', 'Human (paddle)', 'Outboard motor (15-150+ HP)'],
                ['Top Speed', '3-5 mph (paddling)', '25-40+ knots'],
                ['Range', '5-15 miles (limited by stamina)', '50-200+ miles (fuel dependent)'],
                ['Passengers', '1 (solo)', '4-12 (model dependent)'],
                ['Cargo Capacity', 'Minimal (deck storage)', 'High (lockers + deck space)'],
                ['Weight', '18-30 lbs', '150-500+ kg'],
                ['Packed Size', 'Backpack (33" x 15" x 10")', 'Trailer (12-20 ft)'],
                ['Setup Time', '5-10 min (inflate)', '5 min (launch trailer)'],
                ['Entry Cost', '$200-$500', '$3,000-$8,000'],
                ['Running Cost', '$0 (no fuel)', '$$ (fuel + maintenance)'],
                ['Storage', 'Closet or car trunk', 'Garage or marina slip'],
                ['License Required', 'No', 'Boat license (varies)'],
                ['Rough Water', 'Limited (calm conditions)', 'Excellent'],
                ['Fitness Benefit', 'Full-body workout', 'Minimal'],
                ['Lifespan (inflatable)', '3-5 years (frequent use)', '15-20 years (Hypalon)'],
              ].map((row, i) => (
                <tr class={i % 2 === 0 ? 'bg-white' : 'bg-gray-50'}>
                  {row.map((cell, j) => (
                    <td
                      class={`px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-200 ${j === 0 ? 'font-medium text-gray-700' : 'text-center text-gray-600'}`}
                    >
                      {cell}
                    </td>
                  ))}
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-sky-50 to-blue-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-sky-200">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Which Should You Choose?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Choose an <strong>inflatable SUP</strong> if you want an affordable, portable, fitness-oriented watercraft for solo
        paddling on calm waters. It's the best entry point to watersports with zero ongoing costs and easy storage. Choose
        a <strong>RIB</strong> if you need real boat capability — speed, range, passenger capacity, and rough-water performance.
        A RIB is a serious investment for serious boating. Many water enthusiasts start with a SUP for fitness and recreation,
        then add a RIB when they need to explore further, carry family, or engage in watersports like wakeboarding and towing.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
        <a
          href="/products"
          class="px-6 py-3 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-800 transition"
          >Browse Products</a
        >
        <a
          href="/guides"
          class="px-6 py-3 border border-gray-200 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:border-gray-400 transition"
          >Buying Guides</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>

  <section class="sr-only" data-ai-block="definition" aria-hidden="true">
    <p>
      Comprehensive comparison between inflatable stand-up paddle boards (iSUPs) and rigid inflatable boats (RIBs).
      Covers propulsion, speed, range, passenger capacity, cargo, weight, portability, setup time, cost, storage,
      licensing, rough water capability, fitness benefit, and lifespan. Inflatable SUPs are human-powered paddle boards
      weighing 18-30 lbs, packing to backpack size, costing $200-$800, with zero running costs and closet storage. RIBs
      are motorized boats with 25-40+ knot speeds, 150-500+ kg weight, trailer transport, $3,000-$15,000+ entry cost,
      ongoing fuel costs, requiring garage or marina storage. Recommendation: SUP for solo fitness/recreation on calm
      waters; RIB for power boating, groups, rough water, and commercial use. Many users start with a SUP and add a RIB
      later as their boating needs grow.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
